  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/... \nIssued at 200 AM MDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nMoving into the weekend, a cold front will drop across the area\non Saturday, lift back up as a warm front into Sunday, and then\ndrop right back through by Monday. This will be in response to a\ndeep low aloft moving over the PacNW and then across our area\nthrough early next week. With flow remaining southwesterly,\nmonsoonal moisture will continue to increase with PWAT values\n125-150% of normal, possibly even nearing 175% for portions of\nthe Nebraska Panhandle Sunday into Monday. Better instability\nand shear will also support stronger storm activity and may\nsignal the return of strong to severe storms. Into Monday \nmoisture will begin to exit along with these systems, but we\nshould experience the coolest day we've seen since the start of\nsummer, with highs not expected to peak outside of the 60's to\n70's, a sign of fall to come. But into Tuesday ridging will\nbegin to rebound, this time across the southeastern US, with a\nslight warming trend to end the long term.",
